  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the solution of the differential equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If for some&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So the equation becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>So putting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>ln</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;We get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>So on comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}